---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BackgroundGeometry from '../components/BackgroundGeometry.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Tikzfy" hideBackground={true}>
  <BackgroundGeometry />
  <div class="relative z-30 min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-4">
    <div class="w-full max-w-3xl bg-white border-2 border-black p-5 md:p-6 shadow-[4px_4px_0px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,1)] mt-12 relative z-20">
      
      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mb-3 border-b-4 border-black pb-2">
        About the Engine
      </h1>
      
      <div class="space-y-3 font-mono text-xs md:text-sm text-black/80 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-black uppercase tracking-wider">Tikzfy</strong> is an experimental multimodal neural engine designed to bridge the gap between rasterized spatial data and strict mathematical markup. At its core, the system ingests standard image formats and performs algorithmic vectorization. Instead of merely converting pixels to paths, the architecture employs a Vision-Language Model (VLM) fine-tuned specifically on the <span class="bg-black text-white px-1">PGF/TikZ</span> geometry library syntax.
        </p>
        
        <p>
          The pipeline transmutes visual topology—lines, curves, spatial relationships, and embedded text—into a deterministic sequence of LaTeX compiling instructions, guaranteeing structural mathematical precision for seamless integration into academic papers and technical documentation.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 pt-5 border-t-2 border-dashed border-black">
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tighter mb-3 border-b-4 border-black pb-2">
            About the Author
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <p>
              Developed by <strong>Antonio Machuca</strong>, currently pursuing a Double Degree in Mathematics and Software Engineering at Rey Juan Carlos University (Madrid). My academic and technical focus lies at the intersection of quantitative finance, stochastic calculus, and high-performance computation.
            </p>
            
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-1">
              <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/antoniommachuca/" target="_blank" class="flex items-center gap-2 border-2 border-black px-4 py-1.5 hover:bg-black hover:text-white transition-colors font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-xs">
                <span>LI</span> <span class="opacity-70">/in/antoniommachuca</span>
              </a>
              <a href="https://github.com/antoniomachuca" target="_blank" class="flex items-center gap-2 border-2 border-black px-4 py-1.5 hover:bg-black hover:text-white transition-colors font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-xs">
                <span>GH</span> <span class="opacity-70">/antoniomachuca</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="mt-6 flex justify-end">
          <a href="/" class="font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[10px] md:text-xs border-2 border-black px-5 py-2 hover:bg-black hover:text-white transition-colors duration-300">
            ← Return to Compiler
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
